# Sub-market Filter Analysis — Report

## Overview

Tested rolling-average filters (last 5 matches, corners/YC/shots) against 7 betting strategies.
Filter qualifies if: ROI improves >5pp, positive ROI in 4/5 years, n>=15 per year.

**Team name mapping**: backtest_matches uses English names (e.g. "Empoli"), backtest_football_stats uses Russian (e.g. "Эмполи"). Mapped ~155 teams across 5 leagues.
**MLS**: No stats data available — cannot test MLS_BTTS_HOME.
**Data coverage**: SA=1841, EPL=1867, BL1=1483, FL1=1633, PD=1832, RPL=1137 rows.

---

## Results by Strategy

### 1. SA_AWAY_DRAW (SA, draw @ 3.0-4.5, away teams: Empoli/Genoa/Cremonese/Salernitana/Venezia)

| | n | hit% | ROI |
|---|---|---|---|
| **BASELINE** | 137 | 40.1% | +39.8% |
| D: home_corners<=4.5 & away_corners>=3.5 | 41 | 43.9% | +51.0% |
| B: home_shots<=5.0 | 112 | 40.2% | +38.7% |
| A: home_corners<=4.5 | 65 | 40.0% | +37.3% |

Filter D gives +11.2pp ROI improvement — good direction, but n=41 (≈8/year) is too small.
The strategy is already extremely profitable at +39.8% ROI. Any filter that reduces n
makes it harder to bet without meaningfully improving per-bet ROI.

**RECOMMENDATION: NO** — baseline ROI 39.8% is already exceptional; no filter improves enough.

---

### 2. BTTS_YES_CORE EPL (EPL, btts @ 2.00-2.10)

| | n | hit% | ROI |
|---|---|---|---|
| **BASELINE** | 531 | 58.4% | +19.6% |
| F: home_yc>=2 & away_yc>=2 | 141 | 61.7% | +26.3% |
| E: home_shots+away_shots>=10 | 192 | 60.4% | +23.6% |
| D: home_shots>=4 & away_shots>=3 | 351 | 59.0% | +20.7% |

Filter F (+6.7pp) looks best but fails per-year n for 2022 (n=13) and 2025 (n=14).
The year breakdown shows 2023-2024 are strong (hit% 73%, ROI +49%/+40%),
but low-card years suffer.

**RECOMMENDATION: NO** — filter F is close but n too small in low-card years.
Consider a relaxed version: home_yc>=1.5 & away_yc>=1.5 for future testing.

