### 4. FL1_BTTS_DOUBLE (FL1, over2.5 1.6-1.9, btts 2.0-2.1)

| | n | hit% | ROI |
|---|---|---|---|
| **BASELINE** | 182 | 57.1% | +16.8% |
| A: home_yc>=2.0 | 75 | 62.7% | +28.5% |
| C: home_shots>=5 & away_shots>=4 | 66 | 60.6% | +23.9% |
| D: home_shots>=4.5 | 116 | 59.5% | +21.5% |

Filter A gives +11.7pp — strong improvement, but years are too thin:
2021 n=11, 2022 n=13, 2023 n=13 all < 15. ROI flips negative in 2023 (-6%).

**RECOMMENDATION: NO** — per-year n too low despite strong direction.
The 2023 negative year is also a concern (ROI=-6%).

---

### 5. PD_BTTS_DOUBLE (PD, over2.5 1.6-1.9, btts 1.75-1.95)

| | n | hit% | ROI |
|---|---|---|---|
| **BASELINE** | 187 | 61.5% | +15.7% |
| E: home_shots+away_shots>=10 | 61 | 70.5% | +33.6% |
| C: away_shots>=4 & home_corners>=4 | 80 | 67.5% | +27.2% |
| F: home_yc>=2.0 | 113 | 63.7% | +19.8% |

Filter E gives +17.9pp — massive improvement, 5/5 positive years.
But n=61 (≈12/year) fails the n>=15 per year test in 4 of 5 years.
The direction is very strong though — every single year ROI improved significantly:
2021 +46%/+48%, 2022 +18%/+62%, 2023 +31%/+69%, 2024 +11%/+58%, 2025 +58%/+83%.

Filter F (home_yc>=2.0) at n=113 is closer to qualifying but only +4.1pp.

**RECOMMENDATION: NO (borderline)** — filter E has exceptional direction (hit% from 61.5% to 70.5%) but n is too limited.
Suggest collecting more data and retesting once 2026 fills in.
If forced: filter C at n=80 is a reasonable middle ground — 5/5 positive but still n<15/year.

